{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1216683-looking-for-inspiration-spirits","id":1216683,"title":"Looking for inspiration: Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-08T08:50:44-07:00","id":1216683,"title":"Looking for inspiration: Spirits","content":"Whatever your character is a werewolf or a awakened shaman, dealing with spirits is a big part of their activities. As a GM, properly representing such an alien entity with a somewhat blueorange perspective may be difficult.<br /> Is there any novel or resource where I can look for &quot;weird&quot; spirits or similar beings communicating with mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:05:54-07:00","id":1216721,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155772-princess-mononoke-as-werewolf-spirituality-story\">Princess Mononoke is great Shadow Realm ecology example movie</a>. Here is why. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/155772-princess-mononoke-as-werewolf-spirituality-story#post155772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm preparing for running Shadow Realm in our game, I'm rewatching <i>Princess Mononoke</i>. It is official inspiration for <b>Forsaken</b> gameline on Spirits matters and I would like you to clear my understanding of examples in it. Here are my questions:<br /> <br /> 1. <i>Nago</i>, giant boar attacking <i>Ashitaka</i>'s village, is greater spirit ( probably Rank 4, on my eye ) in the flesh of very large boar, correct? So in <b>Werewolf</b> setting, after being slain in this flesh he will return to Shadow Realm, and appears once again after some time, yes?<br /> <br /> 2. If yes <i>Ashitaka</i> really wouldn't kill him, <i>Nago</i> could posses next boar and attack villagers - this is why shamaness of settlement is begging dying <i>Nago</i> to not returning in his wrath, correct? Because she assumes he could return in vengeance?<br /> <br /> 3. <i>Nago</i> is tainted by some corrupt force. I understand that in <b>Werewolf</b> game this would be effect of works from Malejins or Idigams, yes? They could twist the spirit in to something like this? In movie this is said that Wrath burned his body - so Boar Spirit in the beast was driven mad, get Influences of Wrath by some alien source ( probably Malejins ) and changed in to half mad demon, yes?<br /> <br /> 4. If <i>Ashitaka</i> was &quot;cursed&quot; by spiritual poison - is this some kind of Numina, or maybe general power of Corrupted Spirits?<br /> <br /> 5. <i>Moro</i>, Wolf Goddess, is giant she-wof from the same reasons as <i>Nago </i>- they are possesing normal animals for decades, even centuries, and let them grow bodies with they power, yes?<br /> <br /> 6. Kodama are relative weak spirits of trees - so ther are like Rank 1 spirits.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T11:16:08-07:00","id":1216747,"title":"","content":"The animism displayed in Dragon Age hits home pretty close to conceptual spirits as far as I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T12:57:38-07:00","id":1216778,"title":"","content":"I would like to suggest the <a href=\"http://strangers.atrocityland.com/module_primer/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">Strangers</a> as an example of the strange properties or behaviors a spirit may have. May be worth a read for those who enjoy surreal horror or supernatural bestiaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:31:57-07:00","id":1217391,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3028_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3028\" data-vbnamecard=\"3028\">viskarenvisla</a>'s <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?775548-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-The-Seventh-Seal\" target=\"_blank\">actual play <i>The Seventh Seal</i></a> is my go-to reference for evocative handling of spirits. And other werewolfy things. It's excellent and well worth the read for pure entertainment as well.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T12:14:42-07:00","id":1327939,"title":"","content":"Wow <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> thanks, I haven't been around for a while but I didn't see that. I have an interesting surprise though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T13:00:46-07:00","id":1327948,"title":"","content":"I would suggest ye olde monster manual: <i>The Classic of the Mountains &amp; Seas</i>. Its a book from the 4th century BC that describes supernatural beings, genius loci, mythical items and more. There are a lot of things that can be adapted to inspire spirits, rare talens and fetishes, etc. Since its about Chinese mythology, unless your players read a lot of xianxia, its unlikely they will know any of it, adding to the mystery of the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T15:06:54-07:00","id":1328171,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3P5gbHsEnwY\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Check out this video. It is an excellent portrayal of mortals trying to make scientific sense of a fire spirit.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T16:29:54-07:00","id":1328182,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/exploration-log-1689-i\" target=\"_blank\">And this is an example of a lower depth.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}